    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_risk",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "I would separate likelihood from impact, because an unlikely event can still deserve attention if the consequences are severe."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "احتمال رو از اثر جدا می‌کنم چون یک اتفاق کم‌احتمال هم اگر پیامد شدید داشته باشه ارزش توجه داره."
        },
        "intent": "separate_risk_dimensions",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_likelihood",
          "c1_risk_contingency_impact"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_dependency",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "Our largest exposure comes from a single dependency that has no tested fallback."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "بزرگ‌ترین ریسک ما از یک وابستگی واحد میاد که هیچ گزینه پشتیبان تست‌شده‌ای نداره."
        },
        "intent": "identify_exposure",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_exposure",
          "c1_risk_contingency_dependency",
          "c1_risk_contingency_fallback"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_mitigate",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "We cannot remove the risk entirely, but we can mitigate it by reducing how much of the launch depends on one supplier."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نمی‌تونیم ریسک رو کامل حذف کنیم، ولی می‌تونیم با کم کردن وابستگی عرضه به یک تأمین‌کننده کاهش بدیمش."
        },
        "intent": "mitigate_risk",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_mitigate",
          "c1_risk_contingency_dependency"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_threshold",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "We need a threshold that triggers the contingency plan before the original plan has already failed."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "یک آستانه لازم داریم که برنامه جایگزین رو قبل از شکست کامل برنامه اصلی فعال کنه."
        },
        "intent": "set_trigger_threshold",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_threshold",
          "c1_risk_contingency_contingency"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_fallback",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "A fallback is useful only if people know when to use it and it has been tested under realistic conditions."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "گزینه پشتیبان فقط وقتی مفیده که آدم‌ها بدونن کی باید ازش استفاده کنن و در شرایط واقعی تست شده باشه."
        },
        "intent": "evaluate_fallback",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_fallback",
          "c1_risk_contingency_contingency"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_exposure2",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "If the dependency failed tomorrow, our current exposure would affect customer support before core service availability."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "اگر وابستگی فردا از کار بیفته، ریسک فعلی اول پشتیبانی مشتری رو تحت‌تأثیر می‌ذاره نه دسترسی سرویس اصلی رو."
        },
        "intent": "trace_risk_impact",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_dependency",
          "c1_risk_contingency_exposure"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_trade",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Every mitigation has a cost, so the question is whether the reduction in exposure justifies that cost."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "هر کاهش ریسک هزینه‌ای داره، پس سؤال اینه که کاهش در معرض بودن ارزش اون هزینه رو داره یا نه."
        },
        "intent": "weigh_mitigation",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_mitigate",
          "c1_risk_contingency_exposure"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c1_risk_contingency_close",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The contingency should be simple enough to execute under pressure, not merely impressive in a planning document."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "برنامه جایگزین باید اون‌قدر ساده باشه که زیر فشار اجرا بشه، نه فقط روی کاغذ برنامه‌ریزی قشنگ باشه."
        },
        "intent": "close_contingency",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c1_risk_contingency_contingency",
          "c1_risk_contingency_fallback"
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_risk_contingency_mixed_conditionals",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-01",
        "slug": "c1-risk-contingency-mixed-conditionals",
        "title": "Mixed conditionals",
        "rule_summary": "Combine different time references when a past condition has a present result or a present state explains a past outcome.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "وقتی شرط و نتیجه به زمان‌های متفاوت مربوط‌اند از mixed conditional استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "If we had invested earlier, we would be in a stronger position now.",
            "fa": "اگر زودتر سرمایه‌گذاری کرده بودیم، الان موقعیت قوی‌تری داشتیم."
          },
          {
            "en": "If she were less cautious, she might have accepted the offer.",
            "fa": "اگر این‌قدر محتاط نبود، شاید پیشنهاد را قبول کرده بود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_risk_contingency_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-02",
        "slug": "c1-risk-contingency-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_risk_contingency_nominalisation",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-03",
        "slug": "c1-risk-contingency-nominalisation",
        "title": "Nominalisation in formal discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Turn verbs or adjectives into noun phrases to make formal arguments more compact and abstract when appropriate.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در گفتار و نوشتار رسمی، در صورت مناسب بودن فعل یا صفت را به عبارت اسمی تبدیل می‌کنیم تا استدلال فشرده‌تر و انتزاعی‌تر شود."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The rapid expansion of the service created new risks.",
            "fa": "گسترش سریع سرویس ریسک‌های جدیدی ایجاد کرد."
          },
          {
            "en": "A reduction in waiting times would benefit everyone.",
            "fa": "کاهش زمان انتظار به نفع همه خواهد بود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_risk_contingency_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-risk-contingency-01",
        "title": "Risk & Contingency: part 1",
        "setting": "professional workshop",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "jobs",
        "characters": [
          "Ella",
          "Amir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Ella",
            "text": "How would you respond without making the disagreement personal?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور جواب می‌دادی بدون اینکه مخالفت شخصی بشه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Amir",
            "text": "I would separate likelihood from impact, because an unlikely event can still deserve attention if the consequences are severe.",
            "translation_fa": "احتمال رو از اثر جدا می‌کنم چون یک اتفاق کم‌احتمال هم اگر پیامد شدید داشته باشه ارزش توجه داره."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
